  Don't think I'd go along with that completely.  I don't condemn
such things as cheating.  They're just the wrong solution to the 
wrong problem.  (A popular activity among humans, but popularity
isn't everything.)

  Your most important items (i.e. the ones you're carrying in 
inventory) are readily re-identified.  Maybe not completely 
identified but enough to keep going.

  And let's face it, if you went to the trouble of getting 
brain-sucked by a mind-flayer once, you'll probably keep doing
it.  

  So why bother re-learning information you're just going to 
lose again anyway?  When you eventually die to loss of Int, 
that's just the game reflecting reality.


  The problem isn't memory loss from (m)mf.  The problem is 
letting a monster that -

  - has a devastating melee attack
  - gives you early warning that it's on the level
  - doesn't appear in groups of multiple mind-flayers
  - fears Elbereth

  get next to you and attack in melee.  


  I mean, WTF?  Only die-hard (well, die *easy*, if you know what
I mean) proponents of the "Run up and *hit* something!" school 
should have trouble with mind flayers.


  In this light, mind flayers can be seen as just another 
qualifying test in Nethack.  Along with getting poison 
resistance, a luckstone, doing the Quest, passing Medusa, getting
the Candelabrum, and getting the book of the dead.


  In short, if you can't deal with a mindflayer without getting 
brain-sucked, you're not going to ascend anyway.  So don't worry
so much about re-identifying/relearning things.
